1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,288
Two x minus y is zero,

2
00:00:02,288 --> 00:00:04,800
and minus x plus two y is three.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,175
What does solving this look like?

4
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:08,105
The usual picture reads

5
00:00:08,105 --> 00:00:09,205
it row by row:

6
00:00:09,592 --> 00:00:11,342
each equation is a line.

7
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:12,671
The solution is where

8
00:00:12,671 --> 00:00:14,983
the lines cross: x is one,

9
00:00:15,358 --> 00:00:16,246
y is two.

10
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:17,683
Now read the same

11
00:00:17,683 --> 00:00:19,758
system down its columns: two,

12
00:00:20,108 --> 00:00:21,621
minus one goes with x,

13
00:00:21,621 --> 00:00:24,133
and minus one, two goes with y.

14
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:26,595
Each column is an arrow.

15
00:00:26,595 --> 00:00:28,958
The right side, zero, three,

16
00:00:28,958 --> 00:00:30,246
is a target point, b.

17
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:32,970
Which mix of the arrows reaches b?

18
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:35,233
Try one copy of the first arrow,

19
00:00:35,233 --> 00:00:36,958
and two copies of the second.

20
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:39,367
Chain them tip to tail.

21
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:41,692
Two minus two is zero,

22
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:44,417
minus one plus four is three:

23
00:00:44,417 --> 00:00:45,367
exactly b.

24
00:00:45,967 --> 00:00:48,229
And that recipe, one and two,

25
00:00:48,229 --> 00:00:49,242
is the very point

26
00:00:49,242 --> 00:00:50,517
where the lines crossed.

27
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:52,938
So solving A times x equals

28
00:00:52,938 --> 00:00:54,462
b means finding the mix of

29
00:00:54,462 --> 00:00:56,525
A's columns that lands on b.

30
00:00:56,525 --> 00:00:58,150
Unlike crossing lines,

31
00:00:58,150 --> 00:00:59,175
that still works with

32
00:00:59,175 --> 00:01:00,650
a thousand unknowns.
